y Grants and fellowships are \"gift aid\"—financial support that does not need to be repaid. Whether you're an undergraduate seeking need-based aid or a graduate student funding a research project, these resources help reduce your costs so you can focus on your education. Cost of Attendance Cost of Attendance Undergraduate Costs Graduate Costs Net Price Calculator International Cost of Attendance International Cost of Attendance International Cost of Attendance International Cost of Attendance International Undergraduate Costs International Graduate Costs Financial Aid Financial Aid Aid for International Students Grants & Fellowships Grants & Fellowships Loans Loans Pay Your Bill Pay Your Bill Scholarships Scholarships International Student Scholarships International Student Scholarships External Scholarships International Student Scholarships International Student Scholarships C.V. Starr Foundation Scholarship Japan Alumni Chapter Scholarship Scott Schurz Latin American Scholarship BP Peduli Scholarship Bunchana Atthakor Scholarship Eoyang-Lee Fellowship Irving and Lena Lo (ILLO) Scholarship Fund Rising Star Scholarship Global Citizen Scholarship Cost & Aid Cost of Attendance Cost of Attendance Financial Aid Financial Aid Scholarships Scholarships Grants & Fellowships Loans Pay Your Bill Home Cost & Aid Grants & Fellowships Grants: Need-based support for undergraduate students A grant is a form of financial aid that you do not have to repay. Most are awarded to undergraduate students with financial need, which is calculated based on the information you provide on your FAFSA—particularly your Student Aid Index. Explore grant options at Student Central Types of grants Federal grants Explore need-based funding from the U.S. government, including Pell Grants and Federal Supplemental Educational Opportunity Grants (FSEOG). Indiana resident grants Learn about state-funded opportunities specifically for Indiana residents, such as the 21st Century Scholarship and the Frank O'Bannon Grant. Grants specific to IUB students Discover institutional grants provided directly by IU Bloomington to help bridge the gap in your educational costs. Support for graduate students Graduate education often requires specialized funding to support research, teaching, and professional growth. IU provides a robust infrastructure to help graduate students and postdocs find and secure the financial backing they need. Graduate funding Your starting point for discovering the wealth of financial support available specifically for the graduate community. Graduate and postdoctoral professional development Access resources designed to elevate your career prospects, including support for gaining research and teaching skills. GradGrants Center (GGC) Receive free, one-on-one assistance with grant proposal writing and access an extensive database of external funding sources. Diversity Fellows initiative Learn about IU’s commitment to fostering an inclusive environment through specialized fellowship programs for underrepresented students. Fellowships: Research and professional funding Fellowships are a primary way graduate students and high-level researchers fund their work. Internal fellowships come directly from IU, while external fellowships are offered by outside organizations. How to find them: For many internal awards, your individual department or school must nominate you. We encourage you to contact your specific department to learn about their internal deadlines and selection process. Search fellowships and awards IU Bloomington Student Central 408 N. Union Street\nBloomington, IN 47405 812-855-6500 https://studentcentral.indiana.edu Hours Monday: 8am–4:30pm Tuesday: 8:30am–4:30pm Wednesday: 8:30am–4:30pm Thursday: 8:30am–4:30pm Friday: 9am–4:30pm Student Central will be closed on the following days:\nSeptember 7, 2026;\nNovember 26–27, 2026;\nDecember 25, 2026;\nDecember 28–31, 2026;\nMay 31, 2027;\nJune 18, 2027;\nJuly 5, 2027 Legal Accessibility College Scorecard Open to All Privacy Notice Required Disclosures Copyright © The Trustees of Indiana University"
