d Master's Programs Show more section nav three links Browse Accelerated Programs Multidisciplinary Programs Online Programs Browse All Programs Schools Experiential Learning Show more section nav three links Research Opportunities Study Abroad Learning Communities Classes & Registration Academic Calendars Student Records & Grades Show more section nav three links Atlas Portal Degree Requirements & Policies Admissions Show more section nav three links How to Apply Show more section nav three links Freshman Applicants Show more section nav three links Freshman Admission Standards Application Deadlines Test-optional Admission Transfer Applicants Show more section nav three links Transfer Student Admission Standards Application Deadlines Transfer from an IU Campus Graduate Applicants Show more section nav three links Graduate Application Fees Visiting & Non-degree Applicants Adult Applicants Second Undergraduate Applicants Military & Veteran Applicants Application FAQs Admission Paths Show more section nav three links Indiana Residents Visit IU Show more section nav three links High School Counselor Visits Virtual Tour Group Visits Admission Counselors Show more section nav three links Find Your Counselor Precollege Programs Show more section nav three links Find a Precollege Program Information for Parents Planning for IU Show more section nav three links Families Eighth & Ninth Grade Sophomores Juniors Seniors IUBound Programs Show more section nav three links College Access Advising Class Profile Undergraduate Orientation Show more section nav three links Orientation Portal Show more section nav three links Orientation Roadmap Your Orientation Steps Show more section nav three links Attend Orientation Prepare for Advising The Indiana Promise Your First Year Show more section nav three links IU Bucket List Information for Families Travel to Bloomington Show more section nav three links International Travel Arrangements Show more section nav three links Arriving in the U.S. Student Staff Graduate Orientation Steps to Enroll Show more section nav three links Freshman Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Show more section nav three links Freshman Students Transfer Students Graduate Students Intercampus Transfer Students Adult Students Summer Students Cost & Aid Show more section nav three links Cost of Attendance Show more section nav three links Undergraduate Costs Graduate Costs Net Price Calculator International Cost of Attendance Show more section nav three links International Undergraduate Costs International Graduate Costs Financial Aid Show more section nav three links Aid for International Students Scholarships Show more section nav three links International Student Scholarships Show more section nav three links C.V. Starr Foundation Scholarship Japan Alumni Chapter Scholarship Scott Schurz Latin American Scholarship BP Peduli Scholarship Bunchana Atthakor Scholarship Eoyang-Lee Fellowship Irving and Lena Lo (ILLO) Scholarship Fund Rising Star Scholarship Global Citizen Scholarship External Scholarships Grants & Fellowships Loans Pay Your Bill Campus Life Show more section nav three links Campus Traditions Community & Involvement Show more section nav three links Student Organizations Student Ambassadors Athletics & Recreation Housing & Dining Life in Bloomington Campus Events Show more section nav three links America 250 Show more section nav three links Revolution and Reflection Self-Guided Tour Small Grant Recipients Arts and Culture Campus Safety Campus Map, Parking & Transportation Show more section nav three links Getting to Campus Campus Buildings Driving & Parking on Campus Research Show more section nav three links Events & Workshops Innovation & Entrepreneurship Show more section nav three links Innovator Stories Centers, Museums, & Institutes Libraries In the News Student Research Opportunities Student Support Show more section nav three links Academic Advising & Support Career Services & Jobs Show more section nav three links Internships Part-time Jobs Mentorship & Coaching Health & Wellness Show more section nav three links Mental Health Resources Money & Essential Needs Campus Technology Show more section nav three links IU Account Setup Recruit IU Students Alumni & Giving Show more section nav three links Give to IU About Show more section nav three links History Rankings and Statistics Strategic Plan Bloomington Leadership & Administration Show more section nav three links About the Bloomington Chancellor Bloomington Chancellor's Cabinet Bloomington Vice Chancellors Campus Initiatives Show more section nav three links Campus Policy Committee Faculty & Staff Community Show more section nav three links Faculty & Staff Resources For the Glory Newsletter Show more section nav three links IU Foundation IU Foundation Ed Dallis-Comentale Michael Snow Alvin Rosenfeld Roberto Rodriguez Rita Patel Christoph Irmscher and David Polly Brea Perry, Bernice Pescosolido, and Kosali Simon Indiana Daily Student and Arbutus AAAS Fellows IU Debate Team Dana Habeeb Distinguished Professors Sarah Commodore Brian Yanites Brad Fulton Michael Wasserman Jingjing Zhang Pete Kollbaum Indiana University Football Paige Andersson and Rachael Jones McAfee Michel Chaouli Julia Kelson Jeremy Siek Philip Shushkov Monica Nesbitt Kevin Zumbrun Amar Flood Bernice Pescosolido Ore Koren Jacobs School of Music Paul Wright Bridger Ehli David Crandall Roger Innes Faculty Council Reports Show more section nav three links January 27, 2026 Faculty Council report January 13, 2026 Faculty Council report November 18, 2025 Faculty Council report November 4, 2025 Faculty Council report October 14, 2025 Faculty Council report September 23, 2025 Faculty Council report News & Communication Show more section nav three links State of the Campus Show more section nav three links 2026 State of the Campus Search the site Search Close search Career development Support for your career path At IU Bloomington, you have a network of people ready to help you explore options, build skills, and move toward the future you want. From school‑based career centers and mentors to faculty, alumni, and specialized support programs, you’ll find guidance that fits your goals. Back to Academic Advising & Support menu Academic Advising & Support Back to Career Services & Jobs menu Career Services & Jobs Internships Part-time Jobs Mentorship & Coaching Back to Internships menu Internships Back to Part-time Jobs menu Part-time Jobs Back to Health & Wellness menu Health & Wellness Mental Health Resources Back to Money & Essential Needs menu Money & Essential Needs Back to Campus Technology menu Campus Technology IU Account Setup Student Support Academic Advising & Support Career Services & Jobs Career Services & Jobs menu Health & Wellness Health & Wellness menu Money & Essential Needs Campus Technology Campus Technology  menu Recruit IU Students Home Student Support Career Services & Jobs Mentorship & Coaching You don’t have to plan your future alone Career development at IU is intentionally decentralized: every school has its own career center. In addition, Career Exploration & Student Employment (CESE) serves as a central campus resource for students exploring majors, reconsidering their academic path, or seeking part-time student employment. CESE also provides career exploration support for pre-business and pre-nursing students, exploratory majors, and students interested in opportunities beyond their current school. This structure ensures you have access to support from people who understand your academic area, your industry, and the opportunities available to you. Whether you’re choosing a major, preparing for internships, or thinking about graduate school, IU offers multiple ways to get personalized guidance. Start with the resource that feels right for you: Your career path doesn’t have to be linear—and it doesn’t have to be something you figure out on your own. IU gives you a network of people who want to help you succeed. Choose the resource that fits where you are today, and build from there. Career support for every student IU is one of the few universities that provides a dedicated career center for each school, as well as a central career services office through CESE. These teams specialize in the fields you’re studying and the employers who hire in those areas. Career centers can help you: Explore career paths that match your strengths Build resumes, cover letters, and portfolios Practice interviewing and networking Connect with internships and job opportunities Prepare for graduate or professional programs See the full list of IU career centers Still exploring? Check out IU’s career guides to find an overview of potential career fields, related majors at IU, and ways to build experience. Explore career guides Mentoring and coaching programs IU offers mentoring programs that connect you with peers, staff, and professionals who can help you navigate academics, campus life, and career decisions. Undergraduate mentoring Find peer mentors, academic mentors, and identity‑based support programs. Explore mentoring options Find a peer coach Graduate student mentoring Graduate emissaries offer insights on research, faculty relationships, and graduate‑level expectations. Meet your emissary Veteran student support Veteran and military‑connected students can access coaching, advocacy, and transition support. Connect with veteran resources Faculty guidance Your professors can be some of your most valuable mentors. They can help you: Understand career paths in your discipline Explore research opportunities Build academic and professional skills Connect with industry partners or graduate programs Support from IU alumni IU’s alumni network spans industries and continents. Alumni often participate in: Networking events Career panels Mentorship programs Informational interviews Explore the IU Alumni Association Student employment and experience On‑campus jobs and student employment events help you build confidence, earn experience, and develop transferable skills. Discover opportunities and upcoming events IU Bloomington Career Exploration & Student Employment Herman B Wells Library\n1320 E. 10th Street\nBloomington, IN 47405 iucareer@iu.edu (812) 855-5234 Legal Accessibility College Scorecard Open to All Privacy Notice Required Disclosures Copyright © The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
